PokeyATest - RMT music on VBI while loading assets from disk (SIO)
===================================================================

Test bench: a Raster Music Tracker tune keeps playing while files of
2K..16K are loaded from disk, verified (size + checksum) and loaded again,
forever. It counts passes, errors, SIO retries and player timing.

Full guide (Italian): doc/GUIDA.md - RMT player API, asset loading API,
loaders, diagnostics.

Compile / Launch:
-----------------
make            -> build/pokeyatest.atr (MyPicoDos406N, autorun PKATEST.COM)
make run        -> atari800 -xl -pal -nopatchall (NO SIO patch: real POKEY
                   serial timing; ~/.atari800.cfg has ENABLE_SIO_PATCH=1),
                   -run build/disk/PKATEST.COM (started directly, as
                   ../RmtSkeleton: in atari800 the MyPicoDos autorun does not
                   start it), the ATR in D1: for the test files

make SONG=music/xxx.rmt               any mono RMT4 module (instr. speed N:
                                      N player calls per VBI, back to back)
                                      (music/claude_3ch.rmt, claude_3ch_fast.rmt,
                                      claude_3ch_slow.rmt: channels 1-3 only,
                                      claude_3ch_mono_speed_4.rmt: instrument
                                      speed 4, echo of the lead on channel 4,
                                      see ../RmtSkeleton/tools/song3ch.py)
make SONG=music/gemx.sap              a SAP or XEX exported by RITMO / RMT (mono):
                                      its LZSS streams, played by src/lzsplayr.s
                                      (SUBSONG=n: another subtune)
make ASSET_SIZES="2048 7000 16384"    generated test assets, 2048..16384 bytes
                                      (ASSET_SIZES= : none)
your assets: copy them into assets/ (or make ASSETS_DIR=dir): DOS 8.3 names,
1..16384 bytes, they go on the disk and are verified by the test loop too
make clean all DEFS=-DTEST_NOMUSIC    baseline without the player
make clean all DEFS=-DSTOP_ON_ERROR   freeze the screen at the first error

Needs cc65, python3, dir2atr (AtariSIO), atari800.

Keys: L = switch loader (RBL IRQ SIO / OS SIOV)
      S = OS SIO noise on/off (SOUNDR, only meaningful with the OS loader)
      ESC = quit

Files:
------
src/rmtplayr.s   RMT 1.20090108 player (Raster/C.P.U.) ported to ca65, mono,
                 relocatable (tables in the page aligned RMTTAB segment)
src/rmt_feat.inc RMT feature switches (all enabled)
src/lzsplayr.s   player of the LZSS streams of a SAP / XEX exported by RITMO
                 (same interface as rmtplayr.s, from ../RmtSkeleton)
src/rmtvbi.s     player on the immediate VBI + C interface (rmt.h)
src/sio.s        sector read: own IRQ driven SIO driver + OS SIOV version
src/dos2fs.c     read only DOS 2.x/MyDOS filesystem on raw sectors (no DOS)
src/main.c       test program
src/pokeyatest.cfg  atari.cfg + RMTTAB segment
tools/rmt2ca65.py   .rmt -> relocatable ca65 source (pointers rewritten)
tools/sap2ca65.py   .sap / .xex -> relocatable ca65 source (from ../RmtSkeleton)
tools/mkassets.py   test assets + your assets/ -> disk dir + assets.h (sizes, checksums)
tools/atrcheck.py   fails if the ATR has more sectors than the loader supports
tools/atrorder.py   moves PKATEST.COM to the first directory entry (MyPicoDos
                    autorun starts the first file)

How it works:
-------------
1) Immediate VBI (VVBLKI), not deferred: during SIO the OS sets CRITIC and
   skips the deferred VBI. The handler re-enables IRQs (CLI) while the player
   runs, so the serial IRQs are not starved (a byte every ~930 cycles).

2) CLI only if the interrupted code had I=0 (P stacked by the NMI).
   If the NMI hit inside an IRQ handler, a CLI would re-enter it. In that
   case the tick is postponed and run at the tail of the next serial IRQ
   (rmt_irqtick) or at the next VBI: the tempo does not change
   ("late" counter = postponed ticks, "lost" = really lost, must stay 0).

3) During a transfer (rmt_io_begin/rmt_io_end) POKEY channels 3+4 and
   AUDCTL are the 16 bit baud rate generator of the serial port: the player
   does not write AUDF3/AUDC3/AUDF4/AUDC4/AUDCTL and the music goes on with
   channels 1+2 only. Channels 3/4 are programmed with volume 0, so the
   loading is silent (with the OS loader SOUNDR=0 does the same).

4) Loader. The OS SIOV is NOT safe with a heavy VBI player: after the drive
   "Complete" byte the OS re-enables the SERIN IRQ from main code (RECEIV);
   if the VBI runs there the first data byte is lost and the sector comes
   in shifted by one byte - and SIOV can even return status 1 (OK)!
   Press L to see it: "BADLNK" errors. The RBL loader receives ACK,
   Complete, the 128 data bytes and the checksum in a state machine inside
   the VSERIN IRQ handler: nothing depends on main code timing.

Measured in atari800 (PAL, -nopatchall, 19200 baud):
   no music, OS SIOV      : ~960 bytes/s, 0 errors
   music, RBL IRQ loader  : ~880 bytes/s, 0 errors, 0 lost ticks
                            (1216 files in a turbo stress run)
   music, OS SIOV         : shifted sectors, ~70% of the files fail
                            (803 errors vs 315 OK)

Memory: song + biggest asset (the load buffer) must fit in about 28 KB
($2000-$B420). With the default 16 KB test asset the song can be up to ~12 KB;
for a bigger one drop it, e.g. ASSET_SIZES="2048 3500 5120 8000 12288"
(pass SONG= and ASSET_SIZES= to make run too).

Limits: 128 bytes sectors only (SD/ED), drive speed 19200 baud, mono RMT4
modules. Instrument speed N > 1 (1..4): the VBI calls the player N times,
back to back (play_tick in src/rmtvbi.s): tempo and instruments are right,
POKEY changes once per frame, and the player time grows N times.
Checked in atari800 (-pokeyrec): garydenise.rmt (speed 4, from the songs of
RITMO) plays 219 minutes while the test loads files, still in step at the
end (no tick lost); 0.7% of the frames are one frame late (ticks postponed
while the VBI hit an IRQ, caught up), 0.15% are sampled in the middle of the
4 calls. The same song exported by RITMO as SAP (driver Unpatched),
played by lzsplayr.s: 223 minutes (174 loops) while loading, in step, with
the same two kinds of difference only (1.0% late, 0.2% mid-tick).
SAP and RMT need about the same memory (gemx: the program ends at $940D
with the SAP, $93F4 with the .rmt).
